## 4. Keyword Strategy: The Three Concentric Circles

To rank at the top of Google, structure keywords in three rings rather than chasing single high-volume terms.

| Ring | Description | Example Keywords | Expected Volume / Difficulty |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Inner ring (win now) | Long-tail, local, high-intent — low competition, you can rank in 1–3 months | "transport service in Rourkela", "Ranchi to Kolkata truck rate", "return load app India" | Lower volume, very winnable |
| Middle ring (3–6 months) | Regional and category keywords | "PTL transport India", "freight rates Odisha", "e-commerce shipping India" | Medium volume, moderate competition |
| Outer ring (6–12 months) | High-volume national terms that build authority | "trucking India", "logistics marketplace", "freight rates India" | High volume, hard — arrive here via inner-ring authority |

Two tactical notes. First, include **Hinglish and local-language variants** naturally in your content (e.g., "gaadi", "lori/lorry booking", "maal bhejna", "return malai") because a large share of Indian trucker searches is in mixed language. Second, target **Google's AI Overviews and LLM citations** by writing structured, FAQ-style content with clear tables — brands that answer buyer questions in parseable formats are the ones ChatGPT and Perplexity cite when users ask about freight platforms [7].

